TU1NZ COMMERCIAL S11.2-R10 LATENCY STATE-INTEGRITY ROOT CAUSE
Date: 2026-09-22

Scope
-----
Read-only live diagnosis followed by source-only repair. No S8 start, S11
activation, database write, evidence rewrite, Telegram mutation, or server
runtime deployment is part of R10.

Observed evidence
-----------------
- The rolling inventory contained five DIRECT rows.
- All five rows were INTERNAL_TEST / S11_CANARY_RESPONSE /
  INTERNAL_ACCEPTANCE and shared the frozen runtime release and technical run.
- Their bounded technical durations were 439, 424, 425, 452, and 428 ms.
- No REAL row and no UNKNOWN evidence-class row was present.
- The R9 recovery path wrote zero latency rows. The rows originated in the
  failed S11.2 bootstrap technical-evidence writer after START_CANARY.
- S11 remained disabled and CANARY_RED; real acquisition and its baseline were
  unchanged.

Writer and reader path
----------------------
The writer persisted the new S11_CANARY_RESPONSE sample type correctly. The
rollback retained the additive database schema and rows but restored an older
Application reader. That reader did not know the new enum and mapped the rows
to UNKNOWN. Its generic real-user health summary became RED. The Control S9
wrapper then treated that product-level RED as a mandatory S8 runtime gate.

Classification
--------------
H. MULTIPLE_CAUSES
- G. WRITER_READER_SCHEMA_MISMATCH
- D. PRE_CANARY_HEALTH_WRONGLY_REQUIRES_S11_SLO

Repair contract
---------------
- Bind the canonical reader before the one future S8 recovery.
- Expose technical runtime, Canary technical, Canary real-user, and full
  real-user profiles separately.
- Block S8 runtime only on a RED technical runtime profile or a malformed
  profile contract.
- Keep unknown provenance fail-closed.
- Preserve the strict full-product floor and 1000/2000/5000 ms thresholds.
- Keep every historical row unchanged.
- Permit exactly one backup-first future S8 start; restore source contracts and
  stop S8 on failure; never retry Canary.
